---
import { getCollection } from 'astro:content';
import Page from '../../layouts/Page.astro';
import { PUBLISHER, SOFTWARE, WEBSITE, abs, breadcrumbs } from '../../lib/site';

const pages = (await getCollection('compare')).sort((a, b) => a.data.order - b.data.order);
const jsonLd = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@graph': [
    {
      '@type': 'CollectionPage',
      name: 'Compare claude-garage with other ways to run Claude Code',
      '@id': abs('/compare/#page'),
      url: abs('/compare/'),
      isPartOf: WEBSITE,
      about: SOFTWARE,
      publisher: PUBLISHER,
      description: 'Honest comparisons of claude-garage with terminal tabs, tmux on its own, one session at a time, and IDE agent panels.',
    },
    {
      '@type': 'ItemList',
      itemListElement: pages.map((p, i) => ({ '@type': 'ListItem', position: i + 1, name: p.data.title, url: abs(`/compare/${p.id}/`) })),
    },
    breadcrumbs([['Home', '/'], ['Compare', '/compare/']]),
  ],
};
---
<Page title="Compare ways to run many Claude Code sessions" description="Compare claude-garage with terminal tabs, tmux alone, one session at a time and IDE agent panels. Facts, trade-offs and when you do not need it." jsonLd={jsonLd} active="compare">
  <p class="crumbs"><a href="/">Home</a> / Compare</p>
  <h1>Compare ways to run many Claude Code sessions</h1>
  <p class="lead">claude-garage is one way to run several Claude Code sessions. It is not the only way, and it is not always the right one. Each page below lists what you get, what you give up, and when you should skip it.</p>
  <ul class="cards">
    {pages.map((p) => (
      <li><a class="card" href={`/compare/${p.id}/`}><strong>{p.data.title}</strong><span>{p.data.short}</span></a></li>
    ))}
  </ul>
  <h2>How we compare</h2>
  <p>claude-garage is made by the author of this site, so read these pages with that in mind. Every claim about claude-garage comes from its source code and docs. We compare against general workflows, not named products, so nothing here depends on a vendor's current feature list.</p>
  <p>Ready to try it? Read the <a href="/docs/guides/install/">install guide</a>, or see how to <a href="/docs/guides/from-terminal-tabs/">move over from terminal tabs</a>.</p>
</Page>
